-- Delaware General Corporation Law, 8 Del. C. ch. 1 -- piece dg9, LAYER 1: Subchapter X, sections 273 to 277.
-- Dissolution of a joint venture corporation; dissolution before shares are issued or business begun;
-- dissolution generally; dissolution of a nonstock corporation; franchise taxes before dissolution.
--
-- Source: de-code-t8-ch1-2026-10-01.txt, a plain-text rendering made by a converter script from the
-- Delaware Code Online (through 85 Del. Laws, c. 550). It is not the official text. `-- src:N | ...` is
-- line N of that file (an ellipsis means the line goes on).
--
-- Layer 1 takes nobody's point of view: each rule is the relation the text states between the corporation,
-- its stockholders or members, its directors and incorporators, the Court of Chancery and the Secretary of
-- State. A judgment the text hands to the Court is never guessed: the Court "may" act, and the rules say
-- whether the text puts the Court in a position to.
--
-- Section 114(b)(2) lists sections 274 and 275 among those the section 114(a) reading (stockholder as member)
-- does not touch; section 276 and section 311 apply to nonstock corporations by their own words.
-- Out of range, taken as plain inputs: section 103 (piece dg1), section 102(b)(5) (piece dg1), section 391(a)(29)
-- (piece dg11) and chapter 5 of the Law (franchise taxes; not among the inputs).

§ `Subchapter X. Sale of Assets, Dissolution and Winding Up`

§§ `s 273 Dissolution of joint venture corporation having 2 stockholders`

-- Section 273(a): a corporation of this State with only 2 stockholders, each owning 50% of the stock, engaged in
-- a joint venture whose stockholders are unable to agree on discontinuing it; either stockholder may petition the
-- Court of Chancery, "unless otherwise provided in the certificate of incorporation of the corporation or in a
-- written agreement between the stockholders".
-- src:1404 | If the stockholders of a corporation of this State, having only 2 stockholders each of which own 50% of the stock therein, shall be engaged in the prosecution of a joint venture and if such stockholders shall be unable to agree upon the desirability of discontinuing such joint venture and disposing of the assets used in such venture, either stockholder may, unless otherwise provided in the certificate of incorporation of the corporation or in a written agreement between the stockholders, file with the Court of Chancery a petition …
@ref 8 Del. C. § 273(a) (src:1404)
GIVEN `the corporation is a corporation of this State` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the number of stockholders` IS A NUMBER
      `the proportion of the stock owned by the petitioner` IS A NUMBER
      `the proportion of the stock owned by the other stockholder` IS A NUMBER
      `the stockholders are engaged in the prosecution of a joint venture` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the stockholders are unable to agree upon the desirability of discontinuing the joint venture and disposing of the assets used in it` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the certificate of incorporation provides otherwise` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a written agreement between the stockholders provides otherwise` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 273(a) either stockholder may file a petition with the Court of Chancery` MEANS
        `the corporation is a corporation of this State`
    AND `the number of stockholders` EQUALS 2
    AND `the proportion of the stock owned by the petitioner` EQUALS 50%
    AND `the proportion of the stock owned by the other stockholder` EQUALS 50%
    AND `the stockholders are engaged in the prosecution of a joint venture`
    AND `the stockholders are unable to agree upon the desirability of discontinuing the joint venture and disposing of the assets used in it`
    AND (NOT `the certificate of incorporation provides otherwise`)
    AND (NOT `a written agreement between the stockholders provides otherwise`)

-- The petition states the stockholder's desire; "Such petition shall have attached thereto a copy of the
-- proposed plan of discontinuance and distribution and a certificate stating that copies of such petition and
-- plan have been transmitted in writing to the other stockholder and to the directors and officers of such
-- corporation. The petition and certificate shall be executed and acknowledged in accordance with § 103."
-- src:1404 | file with the Court of Chancery a petition stating that it desires to discontinue such joint venture and to dispose of the assets used in such venture in accordance with a plan to be agreed upon by both stockholders or that, if no such plan shall be agreed upon by both stockholders, the corporation be dissolved. …
-- src:1404 | Such petition shall have attached thereto a copy of the proposed plan of discontinuance and distribution and a certificate stating that copies of such petition and plan have been transmitted in writing to the other stockholder and to the directors and officers of such corporation. The petition and certificate shall be executed and acknowledged in accordance with § 103 of this title.
@ref 8 Del. C. § 273(a) (src:1404)
GIVEN `the petition states that the stockholder desires to discontinue the joint venture and dispose of its assets in accordance with a plan to be agreed upon by both stockholders or, if no plan is agreed, that the corporation be dissolved` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a copy of the proposed plan of discontinuance and distribution is attached` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a certificate is attached stating that copies of the petition and plan have been transmitted in writing to the other stockholder and to the directors and officers` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the petition and the certificate were executed and acknowledged in accordance with § 103` IS A BOOLEAN -- out of range: section 103 (piece dg1)
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 273(a) the petition is in order` MEANS
        `the petition states that the stockholder desires to discontinue the joint venture and dispose of its assets in accordance with a plan to be agreed upon by both stockholders or, if no plan is agreed, that the corporation be dissolved`
    AND `a copy of the proposed plan of discontinuance and distribution is attached`
    AND `a certificate is attached stating that copies of the petition and plan have been transmitted in writing to the other stockholder and to the directors and officers`
    AND `the petition and the certificate were executed and acknowledged in accordance with § 103`

-- An agreement of the stockholders, evidenced by a certificate "similarly executed, acknowledged and filed with
-- the Court of Chancery prior to the expiration of such period", extends either period.
-- src:1408 | Either or both of the above periods may be extended by agreement of the stockholders, evidenced by a certificate similarly executed, acknowledged and filed with the Court of Chancery prior to the expiration of such period.
@ref 8 Del. C. § 273(b) (src:1408)
DECLARE `s 273(b) Extension of a period` HAS
    `the date to which the period is extended` IS A DATE
    `the date the certificate of extension was filed with the Court of Chancery` IS A DATE

-- The last day of a period: 3 months (paragraph (b)(1)) or 1 year (paragraph (b)(2)) from the date of the filing of
-- the petition, or the date to which the stockholders extended it by a certificate filed before it expired. A
-- certificate filed on the last day of the period is "prior to the expiration" of it (fork F2 in NOTES.md).
-- src:1406 | (1) Within 3 months of the date of the filing of such petition, a certificate similarly executed and acknowledged stating that they have agreed on such plan, or a modification thereof, and
-- src:1407 | (2) Within 1 year from the date of the filing of such petition, a certificate similarly executed and acknowledged stating that the distribution provided by such plan had been completed,
-- src:1408 | Either or both of the above periods may be extended by agreement of the stockholders, evidenced by a certificate similarly executed, acknowledged and filed with the Court of Chancery prior to the expiration of such period.
@ref 8 Del. C. § 273(b) (src:1406-1408)
GIVEN `the date the petition was filed with the Court of Chancery` IS A DATE
      `the period` IS A Period
      `the extension the stockholders agreed, if any` IS A MAYBE `s 273(b) Extension of a period`
GIVETH A DATE
`s 273(b) the last day of a period, as extended` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the extension the stockholders agreed, if any`
    WHEN NOTHING THEN `the unextended last day`
    WHEN JUST extension THEN
        IF     extension's `the date the certificate of extension was filed with the Court of Chancery` AT MOST `the unextended last day`
           AND extension's `the date to which the period is extended` GREATER THAN `the unextended last day`
        THEN extension's `the date to which the period is extended`
        ELSE `the unextended last day`
    WHERE
        `the unextended last day` MEANS `the date` `the period` `after` `the date the petition was filed with the Court of Chancery`

-- The certificate must be filed by both stockholders within the period: it is filed in time on or before the last day.
-- src:1406 | (1) Within 3 months of the date of the filing of such petition, a certificate similarly executed and acknowledged stating that they have agreed on such plan, or a modification thereof, and
-- src:1407 | (2) Within 1 year from the date of the filing of such petition, a certificate similarly executed and acknowledged stating that the distribution provided by such plan had been completed,
@ref 8 Del. C. § 273(b)(1), (b)(2) (src:1406-1407)
GIVEN `the date both stockholders filed the certificate with the Court of Chancery, if they did` IS A MAYBE DATE
      `the last day of the period, as extended` IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 273(b) the stockholders' certificate was filed within the period` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the date both stockholders filed the certificate with the Court of Chancery, if they did`
    WHEN JUST filed THEN filed AT MOST `the last day of the period, as extended`
    WHEN NOTHING THEN FALSE

-- "Unless both stockholders file ... (1) ... and (2) ...": the Court of Chancery may dissolve the corporation and
-- appoint trustees or receivers when either certificate has not been filed within its period (fork F3 in NOTES.md:
-- the two paragraphs are cumulative, so a failure of either is enough). A period has failed only once its last
-- day has passed. The Court "may": the rule says only that the text puts the Court in a position to.
-- src:1405 | (b) Unless both stockholders file with the Court of Chancery:
-- src:1408 | the Court of Chancery may dissolve such corporation and may by appointment of 1 or more trustees or receivers with all the powers and title of a trustee or receiver appointed under § 279 of this title, administer and wind up its affairs. …
@ref 8 Del. C. § 273(b) (src:1405-1408)
GIVEN `the date of the question` IS A DATE
      `the last day of the 3-month period, as extended` IS A DATE
      `the last day of the 1-year period, as extended` IS A DATE
      `the first certificate was filed within its period` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the second certificate was filed within its period` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 273(b) the Court of Chancery may dissolve the corporation and appoint trustees or receivers to administer and wind up its affairs` MEANS
        (    `the date of the question` GREATER THAN `the last day of the 3-month period, as extended`
         AND (NOT `the first certificate was filed within its period`))
    OR  (    `the date of the question` GREATER THAN `the last day of the 1-year period, as extended`
         AND (NOT `the second certificate was filed within its period`))

-- Section 273(c): for a charitable nonstock corporation the petitioner must give the Attorney General a copy of the
-- petition within 1 week of its filing with the Court of Chancery.
-- src:1409 | (c) In the case of a charitable nonstock corporation, the petitioner shall provide a copy of any petition referred to in subsection (a) of this section to the Attorney General of the State of Delaware within 1 week of its filing with the Court of Chancery.
@ref 8 Del. C. § 273(c) (src:1409)
GIVEN `the kind of corporation` IS A `Kind of corporation`
      `the date the petition was filed with the Court of Chancery` IS A DATE
      `the date the petitioner gave the Attorney General a copy of the petition, if the petitioner did` IS A MAYBE DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 273(c) the petitioner has complied with the duty to provide a copy of the petition to the Attorney General` MEANS
    IF `the kind is a charitable nonstock corporation` `the kind of corporation`
    THEN (CONSIDER `the date the petitioner gave the Attorney General a copy of the petition, if the petitioner did`
          WHEN JUST given THEN given AT MOST (`the date` (`period in weeks` 1) `after` `the date the petition was filed with the Court of Chancery`)
          WHEN NOTHING THEN FALSE)
    ELSE TRUE

§§ `s 274 Dissolution before issuance of shares or beginning of business; procedure`

-- Section 274: "If a corporation has not issued shares or has not commenced the business for which the corporation
-- was organized": the alternatives are alternatives of the text ("or").
-- src:1413 | If a corporation has not issued shares or has not commenced the business for which the corporation was organized, …
@ref 8 Del. C. § 274 (src:1413)
GIVEN `the corporation has issued shares` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the corporation has commenced the business for which it was organized` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 274 the corporation has not issued shares or has not commenced business` MEANS
        NOT `the corporation has issued shares`
    OR  NOT `the corporation has commenced the business for which it was organized`

-- "a majority of the incorporators, or, if directors were named in the certificate of incorporation or have been
-- elected, a majority of the directors, may surrender all of the corporation's rights and franchises". Counts of
-- persons; a count that cannot be a majority answers NOTHING.
-- src:1413 | a majority of the incorporators, or, if directors were named in the certificate of incorporation or have been elected, a majority of the directors, may surrender all of the corporation’s rights and franchises by filing in the office of the Secretary of State a certificate, executed and acknowledged by a majority of the incorporators or directors, …
@ref 8 Del. C. § 274 (src:1413)
GIVEN `directors were named in the certificate of incorporation or have been elected` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the number of incorporators` IS A NUMBER
      `the number of directors` IS A NUMBER
      `the number of those who execute and acknowledge the certificate` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 274 a majority of the incorporators, or of the directors, may surrender the rights and franchises` MEANS
    IF `directors were named in the certificate of incorporation or have been elected`
    THEN `the vote carries` (`a majority of` (`another base named in the provision` "the directors")) `the number of those who execute and acknowledge the certificate` `the number of directors`
    ELSE `the vote carries` (`a majority of` `the incorporators`) `the number of those who execute and acknowledge the certificate` `the number of incorporators`

-- The certificate states: that no shares have been issued or that the business has not been begun; the date of filing
-- of the original certificate of incorporation; that no part of the capital has been paid or, if some, that the amount
-- paid in less necessary expenses has been returned; that if business has begun but no shares issued, all debts have
-- been paid; that if business has not begun but stock certificates were issued, they have been surrendered and
-- cancelled; and that all rights and franchises are surrendered.
-- src:1413 | stating: that no shares of stock have been issued or that the business or activity for which the corporation was organized has not been begun; the date of filing of the corporation’s original certificate of incorporation with the Secretary of State; that no part of the capital of the corporation has been paid, or, if some capital has been paid, that the amount actually paid in for the corporation’s shares, less any part thereof disbursed for necessary expenses, has been returned to those entitled thereto; that if the corporation has begun business but it has not issued shares, all debts of the corporation have been paid; that if the corporation has not begun business but has issued stock certificates, all issued stock certificates, if any, have been surrendered and cancelled; and that all rights and franchises of the corporation are surrendered. …
@ref 8 Del. C. § 274 (src:1413)
DECLARE `s 274 Certificate of surrender` HAS
    `statement that no shares have been issued or that the business has not been begun` IS A BOOLEAN
    `statement of the date of filing of the original certificate of incorporation` IS A BOOLEAN
    `statement that no part of the capital has been paid or that the amount paid in, less necessary expenses, has been returned` IS A BOOLEAN
    `statement that all debts of the corporation have been paid` IS A BOOLEAN
    `statement that all issued stock certificates have been surrendered and cancelled` IS A BOOLEAN
    `statement that all rights and franchises of the corporation are surrendered` IS A BOOLEAN

-- src:1413 | that if the corporation has begun business but it has not issued shares, all debts of the corporation have been paid; that if the corporation has not begun business but has issued stock certificates, all issued stock certificates, if any, have been surrendered and cancelled; …
@ref 8 Del. C. § 274 (src:1413)
GIVEN `the certificate` IS A `s 274 Certificate of surrender`
      `the corporation has begun business but has not issued shares` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the corporation has not begun business but has issued stock certificates` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 274 the certificate of surrender states what the section requires` MEANS
        `the certificate`'s `statement that no shares have been issued or that the business has not been begun`
    AND `the certificate`'s `statement of the date of filing of the original certificate of incorporation`
    AND `the certificate`'s `statement that no part of the capital has been paid or that the amount paid in, less necessary expenses, has been returned`
    AND ((NOT `the corporation has begun business but has not issued shares`) OR `the certificate`'s `statement that all debts of the corporation have been paid`)
    AND ((NOT `the corporation has not begun business but has issued stock certificates`) OR `the certificate`'s `statement that all issued stock certificates have been surrendered and cancelled`)
    AND `the certificate`'s `statement that all rights and franchises of the corporation are surrendered`

-- "Upon such certificate becoming effective in accordance with § 103 of this title, the corporation shall be dissolved."
-- src:1413 | Upon such certificate becoming effective in accordance with § 103 of this title, the corporation shall be dissolved.
@ref 8 Del. C. § 274 (src:1413)
GIVEN `the certificate has become effective in accordance with § 103` IS A BOOLEAN -- out of range: section 103 (piece dg1)
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 274 the corporation is dissolved by the certificate of surrender` MEANS
    `the certificate has become effective in accordance with § 103`

§§ `s 275 Dissolution generally; procedure`

-- Section 275(a): the board, after adopting a resolution by "a majority of the whole board at any meeting called for
-- that purpose", causes notice of the adoption and of a meeting of stockholders to be given to each stockholder
-- entitled to vote as of the record date. The counts are of directors; the whole board is the count the caller gives.
-- src:1417 | the board, after the adoption of a resolution to that effect by a majority of the whole board at any meeting called for that purpose, …
@ref 8 Del. C. § 275(a) (src:1417)
GIVEN `the number of directors who voted for the resolution` IS A NUMBER
      `the number of directors constituting the whole board` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 275(a) the board adopted the resolution to dissolve by a majority of the whole board` MEANS
    `the vote carries` (`a majority of` `the whole board`) `the number of directors who voted for the resolution` `the number of directors constituting the whole board`

-- src:1417 | shall cause notice of the adoption of the resolution and of a meeting of stockholders to take action upon the resolution to be given to each stockholder entitled to vote thereon as of the record date for determining the stockholders entitled to notice of the meeting.
@ref 8 Del. C. § 275(a) (src:1417)
GIVEN `the meeting of the board was called for the purpose of the resolution` IS A BOOLEAN
      `notice of the adoption of the resolution and of the meeting of stockholders was given to each stockholder entitled to vote as of the record date` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 275(a) the board has done what the subsection requires before the stockholders vote` MEANS
        `the meeting of the board was called for the purpose of the resolution`
    AND `notice of the adoption of the resolution and of the meeting of stockholders was given to each stockholder entitled to vote as of the record date`

-- Section 275(b): "If a majority of the outstanding stock of the corporation entitled to vote thereon shall vote for
-- the proposed dissolution": more than half the votes (section 212(a), out of range, makes the counts votes).
-- src:1418 | If a majority of the outstanding stock of the corporation entitled to vote thereon shall vote for the proposed dissolution, …
@ref 8 Del. C. § 275(b) (src:1418)
GIVEN `the votes for the proposed dissolution` IS A NUMBER
      `the votes of the outstanding stock entitled to vote thereon` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 275(b) a majority of the outstanding stock entitled to vote has voted for the proposed dissolution` MEANS
    `the vote carries` (`a majority of` `the outstanding stock entitled to vote`) `the votes for the proposed dissolution` `the votes of the outstanding stock entitled to vote thereon`

-- Section 275(c): "without action of the directors if all the stockholders entitled to vote thereon shall consent
-- in writing": all of them, so the proportion is 1 and is reached.
-- src:1419 | Dissolution of a corporation may also be authorized without action of the directors if all the stockholders entitled to vote thereon shall consent in writing …
@ref 8 Del. C. § 275(c) (src:1419)
GIVEN `the number of stockholders entitled to vote who consented in writing` IS A NUMBER
      `the number of stockholders entitled to vote` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 275(c) all the stockholders entitled to vote have consented in writing to the dissolution` MEANS
    `the vote carries` (`at least` 1 (`another base named in the provision` "the stockholders entitled to vote thereon")) `the number of stockholders entitled to vote who consented in writing` `the number of stockholders entitled to vote`

-- Dissolution is authorized in accordance with section 275 by either route: the board's resolution and the
-- stockholders' vote under (a) and (b), or the written consent of all stockholders under (c).
-- src:1418 | If a majority of the outstanding stock of the corporation entitled to vote thereon shall vote for the proposed dissolution, a certification of dissolution shall be filed with the Secretary of State pursuant to subsection (d) of this section.
-- src:1419 | Dissolution of a corporation may also be authorized without action of the directors if all the stockholders entitled to vote thereon shall consent in writing and a certificate of dissolution shall be filed with the Secretary of State pursuant to subsection (d) of this section.
@ref 8 Del. C. § 275(b), (c) (src:1418-1419)
GIVEN `the resolution of the board was adopted by a majority of the whole board` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the board did what s 275(a) requires before the stockholders voted` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a majority of the outstanding stock entitled to vote voted for the proposed dissolution` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `all the stockholders entitled to vote consented in writing` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 275 the dissolution is authorized in accordance with this section` MEANS
    CONSIDER `all the stockholders entitled to vote consented in writing`
    WHEN JUST TRUE THEN JUST TRUE
    OTHERWISE
        CONSIDER `the resolution of the board was adopted by a majority of the whole board`
        WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING
        WHEN JUST board THEN
            CONSIDER `a majority of the outstanding stock entitled to vote voted for the proposed dissolution`
            WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING
            WHEN JUST stockholders THEN JUST (board AND `the board did what s 275(a) requires before the stockholders voted` AND stockholders)

-- Section 275(d): the certificate of dissolution is executed, acknowledged, filed and effective in accordance with
-- section 103, and sets forth six things.
-- src:1420 | (d) If dissolution is authorized in accordance with this section, a certificate of dissolution shall be executed, acknowledged and filed, and shall become effective, in accordance with § 103 of this title. …
-- src:1421 | (1) The name of the corporation;
-- src:1422 | (2) The date dissolution was authorized;
-- src:1423 | (3) That the dissolution has been authorized by the board of directors and stockholders of the corporation, in accordance with subsections (a) and (b) of this section, or that the dissolution has been authorized by all of the stockholders of the corporation entitled to vote on a dissolution, in accordance with subsection (c) of this section;
-- src:1424 | (4) The names and addresses of the directors and officers of the corporation;
-- src:1425 | (5) The date of filing of the corporation’s original certificate of incorporation with the Secretary of State; and
-- src:1426 | (6) The agreement required by subsection (i) of this section.
@ref 8 Del. C. § 275(d) (src:1420-1426)
DECLARE `s 275(d) Certificate of dissolution` HAS
    `statement of the name of the corporation` IS A BOOLEAN
    `statement of the date dissolution was authorized` IS A BOOLEAN
    `statement that the dissolution was authorized by the board of directors and stockholders under subsections (a) and (b), or by all of the stockholders entitled to vote under subsection (c)` IS A BOOLEAN
    `statement of the names and addresses of the directors and officers` IS A BOOLEAN
    `statement of the date of filing of the original certificate of incorporation` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the agreement required by subsection (i)` IS A BOOLEAN

-- src:1420 | (d) If dissolution is authorized in accordance with this section, a certificate of dissolution shall be executed, acknowledged and filed, and shall become effective, in accordance with § 103 of this title. Such certificate of dissolution shall set forth:
-- src:1421 | (1) The name of the corporation;
-- src:1422 | (2) The date dissolution was authorized;
-- src:1423 | (3) That the dissolution has been authorized by the board of directors and stockholders of the corporation, in accordance with subsections (a) and (b) of this section, or that the dissolution has been authorized by all of the stockholders of the corporation entitled to vote on a dissolution, in accordance with subsection (c) of this section;
-- src:1424 | (4) The names and addresses of the directors and officers of the corporation;
-- src:1425 | (5) The date of filing of the corporation’s original certificate of incorporation with the Secretary of State; and
-- src:1426 | (6) The agreement required by subsection (i) of this section.
@ref 8 Del. C. § 275(d) (src:1420-1426)
GIVEN `the certificate` IS A `s 275(d) Certificate of dissolution`
      `the certificate was executed, acknowledged and filed in accordance with § 103` IS A BOOLEAN -- out of range: section 103 (piece dg1)
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 275(d) the certificate of dissolution is in order` MEANS
        `the certificate was executed, acknowledged and filed in accordance with § 103`
    AND `the certificate`'s `statement of the name of the corporation`
    AND `the certificate`'s `statement of the date dissolution was authorized`
    AND `the certificate`'s `statement that the dissolution was authorized by the board of directors and stockholders under subsections (a) and (b), or by all of the stockholders entitled to vote under subsection (c)`
    AND `the certificate`'s `statement of the names and addresses of the directors and officers`
    AND `the certificate`'s `statement of the date of filing of the original certificate of incorporation`
    AND `the certificate`'s `the agreement required by subsection (i)`

-- Section 275(e): the resolution authorizing a proposed dissolution "may provide that notwithstanding authorization or
-- consent ... the board of directors or governing body may abandon such proposed dissolution without further action
-- by the stockholders or members". Where the resolution so provides the power exists; where it does not the
-- subsection says nothing.
-- src:1427 | (e) The resolution authorizing a proposed dissolution may provide that notwithstanding authorization or consent to the proposed dissolution by the stockholders, or the members of a nonstock corporation pursuant to § 276 of this title, the board of directors or governing body may abandon such proposed dissolution without further action by the stockholders or members.
@ref 8 Del. C. § 275(e) (src:1427)
GIVEN `the resolution authorizing the proposed dissolution provides that the board of directors or governing body may abandon it without further action by the stockholders or members` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 275(e) the board or governing body may abandon the proposed dissolution without further action by the stockholders or members` MEANS
    IF `the resolution authorizing the proposed dissolution provides that the board of directors or governing body may abandon it without further action by the stockholders or members`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING

-- Section 275(f): a corporation whose certificate of incorporation limits its duration to a specified date in
-- accordance with section 102(b)(5) (out of range: piece dg1) files its certificate of dissolution "within 90 days
-- before such specified date", and it becomes effective on that date. Reading taken (fork F4): the window runs from
-- the 90th day before the specified date to the day before it; a filing on the specified date itself is not "before" it.
-- src:1428 | (f) If a corporation has included in its certificate of incorporation a provision limiting the duration of its existence to a specified date in accordance with § 102(b)(5) of this title, a certificate of dissolution shall be executed, acknowledged and filed in accordance with § 103 of this title within 90 days before such specified date and shall become effective on such specified date. …
@ref 8 Del. C. § 275(f) (src:1428)
`s 275(f) the longest time before the specified date within which the certificate of dissolution is filed` MEANS `period in days` 90

@ref 8 Del. C. § 275(f) (src:1428)
GIVEN `the date specified in the certificate of incorporation limiting the duration of the corporation's existence` IS A DATE -- out of range: section 102(b)(5) (piece dg1)
      `the date the certificate of dissolution is filed` IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 275(f) the certificate of dissolution is filed within 90 days before the specified date` MEANS
        `the date the certificate of dissolution is filed` AT LEAST (`the date` `s 275(f) the longest time before the specified date within which the certificate of dissolution is filed` `before` `the date specified in the certificate of incorporation limiting the duration of the corporation's existence`)
    AND `the date the certificate of dissolution is filed` LESS THAN `the date specified in the certificate of incorporation limiting the duration of the corporation's existence`

-- src:1429 | (1) The name of the corporation;
-- src:1430 | (2) The date specified in the corporation’s certificate of incorporation limiting the duration of its existence;
-- src:1431 | (3) The names and addresses of the directors and officers of the corporation;
-- src:1432 | (4) The date of filing of the corporation’s original certificate of incorporation with the Secretary of State; and
-- src:1433 | (5) The agreement required by subsection (i) of this section.
@ref 8 Del. C. § 275(f) (src:1429-1433)
DECLARE `s 275(f) Certificate of dissolution on expiry` HAS
    `statement of the name of the corporation` IS A BOOLEAN
    `statement of the date specified in the certificate of incorporation limiting the duration of the corporation's existence` IS A BOOLEAN
    `statement of the names and addresses of the directors and officers` IS A BOOLEAN
    `statement of the date of filing of the original certificate of incorporation` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the agreement required by subsection (i)` IS A BOOLEAN

-- src:1429 | (1) The name of the corporation;
-- src:1430 | (2) The date specified in the corporation’s certificate of incorporation limiting the duration of its existence;
-- src:1431 | (3) The names and addresses of the directors and officers of the corporation;
-- src:1432 | (4) The date of filing of the corporation’s original certificate of incorporation with the Secretary of State; and
-- src:1433 | (5) The agreement required by subsection (i) of this section.
@ref 8 Del. C. § 275(f) (src:1429-1433)
GIVEN `the certificate` IS A `s 275(f) Certificate of dissolution on expiry`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 275(f) the certificate of dissolution on expiry states what the subsection requires` MEANS
        `the certificate`'s `statement of the name of the corporation`
    AND `the certificate`'s `statement of the date specified in the certificate of incorporation limiting the duration of the corporation's existence`
    AND `the certificate`'s `statement of the names and addresses of the directors and officers`
    AND `the certificate`'s `statement of the date of filing of the original certificate of incorporation`
    AND `the certificate`'s `the agreement required by subsection (i)`

-- "The failure to timely file a certificate of dissolution ... shall not affect the expiration of such corporation's
-- existence on the date specified ... and shall not eliminate the requirement to file a certificate of dissolution".
-- Whether the corporation's existence has expired on a date depends on the specified date alone, never on a filing.
-- src:1434 | The failure to timely file a certificate of dissolution pursuant to this subsection with respect to any corporation shall not affect the expiration of such corporation’s existence on the date specified in its certificate of incorporation pursuant to § 102(b)(5) of this title and shall not eliminate the requirement to file a certificate of dissolution as contemplated by this subsection. …
@ref 8 Del. C. § 275(f) (src:1434)
GIVEN `the date specified in the certificate of incorporation limiting the duration of the corporation's existence` IS A DATE
      `the date of the question` IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 275(f) the corporation's existence has expired on the specified date` MEANS
    `the date of the question` AT LEAST `the date specified in the certificate of incorporation limiting the duration of the corporation's existence`

@ref 8 Del. C. § 275(f) (src:1434)
GIVEN `no certificate of dissolution has been filed` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 275(f) the requirement to file a certificate of dissolution remains` MEANS
    `no certificate of dissolution has been filed`

-- "If a certificate of good standing is issued by the Secretary of State after the date specified ..., such
-- certificate of good standing shall be of no force or effect." For one issued on or before that date the sentence
-- says nothing.
-- src:1434 | If a certificate of good standing is issued by the Secretary of State after the date specified in a corporation’s certificate of incorporation pursuant to § 102(b)(5) of this title, such certificate of good standing shall be of no force or effect.
@ref 8 Del. C. § 275(f) (src:1434)
GIVEN `the date specified in the certificate of incorporation limiting the duration of the corporation's existence` IS A DATE
      `the date the certificate of good standing was issued` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 275(f) a certificate of good standing issued by the Secretary of State has force or effect` MEANS
    IF `the date the certificate of good standing was issued` GREATER THAN `the date specified in the certificate of incorporation limiting the duration of the corporation's existence`
    THEN JUST FALSE
    ELSE NOTHING

-- Section 275(g): "A corporation shall be dissolved upon the earlier of: (1) The date specified in such corporation's
-- certificate of incorporation ...; or (2) The effectiveness in accordance with § 103 ... of a certificate of
-- dissolution". With neither, the subsection dissolves nothing: NOTHING.
-- src:1435 | (g) A corporation shall be dissolved upon the earlier of:
-- src:1436 | (1) The date specified in such corporation’s certificate of incorporation pursuant to § 102(b)(5) of this title; or
-- src:1437 | (2) The effectiveness in accordance with § 103 of this title of a certificate of dissolution filed in accordance with this section.
@ref 8 Del. C. § 275(g) (src:1435-1437)
GIVEN `the date specified in the certificate of incorporation limiting the duration of the corporation's existence, if there is one` IS A MAYBE DATE
      `the date a certificate of dissolution becomes effective in accordance with § 103, if one does` IS A MAYBE DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
`s 275(g) the date on which the corporation is dissolved` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the date specified in the certificate of incorporation limiting the duration of the corporation's existence, if there is one`
    WHEN JUST specified THEN
        CONSIDER `the date a certificate of dissolution becomes effective in accordance with § 103, if one does`
        WHEN JUST effective THEN JUST (IF specified AT MOST effective THEN specified ELSE effective)
        WHEN NOTHING THEN JUST specified
    WHEN NOTHING THEN
        CONSIDER `the date a certificate of dissolution becomes effective in accordance with § 103, if one does`
        WHEN JUST effective THEN JUST effective
        WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING

-- Section 275(h): the registered agent's authority and responsibilities end when the filing of the certificate of
-- dissolution is effective, "except with respect to service of process received by the registered agent before
-- the effectiveness of the filing".
-- src:1438 | (h) The authority and responsibilities of the registered agent of a dissolved corporation terminate at the time of the effectiveness of the filing of the certificate of dissolution, except with respect to service of process received by the registered agent before the effectiveness of the filing of the certificate of dissolution.
@ref 8 Del. C. § 275(h) (src:1438)
GIVEN `the filing of the certificate of dissolution is effective` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the registered agent received the process before the filing became effective` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 275(h) the registered agent's authority and responsibilities continue with respect to the process` MEANS
        NOT `the filing of the certificate of dissolution is effective`
    OR  `the registered agent received the process before the filing became effective`

-- Section 275(i): what the dissolving corporation agrees and appoints.
-- src:1439 | The dissolving corporation shall agree that it may be served with process in this State in any proceeding for enforcement of any obligation of the dissolved corporation, and shall irrevocably appoint, with the appointment effective on and after the effectiveness of the filing of the certificate of dissolution, the Secretary of State as its agent to accept service of process in any such suit or other proceedings and shall specify the address to which a copy of such process shall be sent by the Secretary of State. …
@ref 8 Del. C. § 275(i) (src:1439)
GIVEN `the corporation agrees that it may be served with process in this State in any proceeding for enforcement of any obligation of the dissolved corporation` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the corporation irrevocably appoints the Secretary of State as its agent to accept service of process, effective on and after the effectiveness of the filing` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the corporation specifies the address to which a copy of the process is to be sent` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 275(i) the dissolving corporation has made the agreement and appointment the subsection requires` MEANS
        `the corporation agrees that it may be served with process in this State in any proceeding for enforcement of any obligation of the dissolved corporation`
    AND `the corporation irrevocably appoints the Secretary of State as its agent to accept service of process, effective on and after the effectiveness of the filing`
    AND `the corporation specifies the address to which a copy of the process is to be sent`

-- "Process may be served upon the Secretary of State under this subsection by means of electronic transmission but
-- only as prescribed by the Secretary of State." The Secretary of State's power to "issue such rules and
-- regulations with respect to such service" is regulation-making machinery and is not encoded (NOTES.md, coverage).
-- src:1439 | Process may be served upon the Secretary of State under this subsection by means of electronic transmission but only as prescribed by the Secretary of State. …
@ref 8 Del. C. § 275(i) (src:1439)
GIVEN `the process is served by electronic transmission` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the electronic transmission is as prescribed by the Secretary of State` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 275(i) the service of process on the Secretary of State is by a permitted means` MEANS
    (NOT `the process is served by electronic transmission`) OR `the electronic transmission is as prescribed by the Secretary of State`

-- "the Secretary of State shall forthwith notify the dissolved corporation thereof by letter, directed to such
-- dissolved corporation at its address so specified, unless such dissolved corporation shall have designated in
-- writing to the Secretary of State a different address for such purpose, in which case it shall be sent to the last
-- address so designated."
-- src:1439 | In the event of such service upon the Secretary of State in accordance with this subsection, the Secretary of State shall forthwith notify the dissolved corporation thereof by letter, directed to such dissolved corporation at its address so specified, unless such dissolved corporation shall have designated in writing to the Secretary of State a different address for such purpose, in which case it shall be sent to the last address so designated. …
@ref 8 Del. C. § 275(i) (src:1439)
GIVEN `the address the corporation specified for the copy of the process` IS A STRING
      `the addresses the dissolved corporation later designated in writing to the Secretary of State, in the order designated` IS A LIST OF STRING
GIVETH A STRING
`s 275(i) the address to which the Secretary of State sends the letter` MEANS
    CONSIDER reverse `the addresses the dissolved corporation later designated in writing to the Secretary of State, in the order designated`
    WHEN EMPTY THEN `the address the corporation specified for the copy of the process`
    WHEN latest FOLLOWED BY earlier THEN latest

-- "Such letter shall be sent by a mail or courier service that includes a record of mailing or deposit with the
-- courier and a record of delivery evidenced by the signature of the recipient. Such letter shall enclose a copy of
-- the process and any other papers served on the Secretary of State pursuant to this subsection."
-- src:1439 | Such letter shall be sent by a mail or courier service that includes a record of mailing or deposit with the courier and a record of delivery evidenced by the signature of the recipient. Such letter shall enclose a copy of the process and any other papers served on the Secretary of State pursuant to this subsection. …
@ref 8 Del. C. § 275(i) (src:1439)
GIVEN `the letter is sent by a mail or courier service` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the service includes a record of mailing or deposit with the courier` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the service includes a record of delivery evidenced by the signature of the recipient` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the letter encloses a copy of the process and any other papers served on the Secretary of State` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 275(i) the letter from the Secretary of State is sent as the subsection requires` MEANS
        `the letter is sent by a mail or courier service`
    AND `the service includes a record of mailing or deposit with the courier`
    AND `the service includes a record of delivery evidenced by the signature of the recipient`
    AND `the letter encloses a copy of the process and any other papers served on the Secretary of State`

-- "It shall be the duty of the plaintiff in the event of such service to serve process and any other papers in
-- duplicate, to notify the Secretary of State that service is being effected pursuant to this subsection and to pay
-- the Secretary of State a fee as prescribed under § 391(a)(29) of this title".
-- src:1439 | It shall be the duty of the plaintiff in the event of such service to serve process and any other papers in duplicate, to notify the Secretary of State that service is being effected pursuant to this subsection and to pay the Secretary of State a fee as prescribed under § 391(a)(29) of this title for the use of the State …
@ref 8 Del. C. § 275(i) (src:1439)
GIVEN `the plaintiff served the process and any other papers in duplicate` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the plaintiff notified the Secretary of State that service is being effected pursuant to section 275(i)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the plaintiff paid the Secretary of State the fee prescribed under § 391(a)(29)` IS A BOOLEAN -- out of range: section 391(a)(29) (piece dg11)
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 275(i) the plaintiff has done what the subsection makes the plaintiff's duty` MEANS
        `the plaintiff served the process and any other papers in duplicate`
    AND `the plaintiff notified the Secretary of State that service is being effected pursuant to section 275(i)`
    AND `the plaintiff paid the Secretary of State the fee prescribed under § 391(a)(29)`

-- "which sum shall be taxed as part of the costs in the proceeding, if the plaintiff shall prevail therein." If the
-- plaintiff does not prevail the sentence says nothing.
-- src:1439 | which sum shall be taxed as part of the costs in the proceeding, if the plaintiff shall prevail therein. …
@ref 8 Del. C. § 275(i) (src:1439)
GIVEN `the plaintiff prevails in the proceeding` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 275(i) the fee is taxed as part of the costs in the proceeding` MEANS
    IF `the plaintiff prevails in the proceeding` THEN JUST TRUE ELSE NOTHING

-- "The Secretary of State shall maintain an alphabetical record of any such service setting forth the name of the
-- plaintiff and the defendant, the title, docket number and nature of the proceeding in which process has been
-- served, the fact that service has been effected pursuant to this subsection, the return date thereof, and the day
-- and hour service was made."
-- src:1439 | The Secretary of State shall maintain an alphabetical record of any such service setting forth the name of the plaintiff and the defendant, the title, docket number and nature of the proceeding in which process has been served, the fact that service has been effected pursuant to this subsection, the return date thereof, and the day and hour service was made. …
@ref 8 Del. C. § 275(i) (src:1439)
DECLARE `s 275(i) Record of service on the Secretary of State` HAS
    `entry of the name of the plaintiff` IS A BOOLEAN
    `entry of the name of the defendant` IS A BOOLEAN
    `entry of the title of the proceeding` IS A BOOLEAN
    `entry of the docket number` IS A BOOLEAN
    `entry of the nature of the proceeding` IS A BOOLEAN
    `entry of the fact that service has been effected pursuant to the subsection` IS A BOOLEAN
    `entry of the return date` IS A BOOLEAN
    `entry of the day and hour service was made` IS A BOOLEAN

-- src:1439 | The Secretary of State shall maintain an alphabetical record of any such service setting forth the name of the plaintiff and the defendant, the title, docket number and nature of the proceeding in which process has been served, the fact that service has been effected pursuant to this subsection, the return date thereof, and the day and hour service was made. …
@ref 8 Del. C. § 275(i) (src:1439)
GIVEN `the record` IS A `s 275(i) Record of service on the Secretary of State`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 275(i) the Secretary of State's record of a service sets forth what the subsection requires` MEANS
        `the record`'s `entry of the name of the plaintiff`
    AND `the record`'s `entry of the name of the defendant`
    AND `the record`'s `entry of the title of the proceeding`
    AND `the record`'s `entry of the docket number`
    AND `the record`'s `entry of the nature of the proceeding`
    AND `the record`'s `entry of the fact that service has been effected pursuant to the subsection`
    AND `the record`'s `entry of the return date`
    AND `the record`'s `entry of the day and hour service was made`

-- "The Secretary of State shall not be required to retain such information longer than 5 years from receipt of the
-- service of process." Retention is required through the 5th anniversary of receipt; after it, not.
-- src:1439 | The Secretary of State shall not be required to retain such information longer than 5 years from receipt of the service of process.
@ref 8 Del. C. § 275(i) (src:1439)
GIVEN `the date the Secretary of State received the service of process` IS A DATE
      `the date of the question` IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 275(i) the Secretary of State is required to retain the record` MEANS
    `the date of the question` AT MOST (`the date` (`period in years` 5) `after` `the date the Secretary of State received the service of process`)

§§ `s 276 Dissolution of nonstock corporation; procedure`

-- Section 276(a): the governing body does what the board does, and the members entitled to vote do what the
-- stockholders do, under section 275. If no member is entitled to vote, the dissolution is authorized at a meeting
-- of the governing body "upon the adoption of a resolution to dissolve by the vote of a majority of members of its
-- governing body then in office".
-- src:1443 | Whenever it shall be desired to dissolve any nonstock corporation, the governing body shall perform all the acts necessary for dissolution which are required by § 275 of this title to be performed by the board of directors of a corporation having capital stock. …
-- src:1443 | If there is no member entitled to vote thereon, the dissolution of the corporation shall be authorized at a meeting of the governing body, upon the adoption of a resolution to dissolve by the vote of a majority of members of its governing body then in office. …
@ref 8 Del. C. § 276(a) (src:1443)
GIVEN `the number of members of the governing body who voted for the resolution to dissolve` IS A NUMBER
      `the number of members of the governing body then in office` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 276(a) a majority of the members of the governing body then in office voted for the resolution to dissolve` MEANS
    `the vote carries` (`a majority of` `the directors then in office`) `the number of members of the governing body who voted for the resolution to dissolve` `the number of members of the governing body then in office`

-- src:1443 | If any members of a nonstock corporation are entitled to vote for the election of members of its governing body or are entitled to vote for dissolution under the certificate of incorporation or the bylaws of such corporation, such members shall perform all the acts necessary for dissolution which are contemplated by § 275 of this title to be performed by the stockholders of a corporation having capital stock, including dissolution without action of the members of the governing body if all the members of the corporation entitled to vote thereon shall consent in writing and a certificate of dissolution shall be filed with the Secretary of State pursuant to § 275(d) of this title. …
@ref 8 Del. C. § 276(a) (src:1443)
GIVEN `any members are entitled to vote for the election of members of the governing body or for dissolution under the certificate of incorporation or the bylaws` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the dissolution is authorized in accordance with section 275 as performed by the governing body and the members` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the dissolution is authorized by the vote of a majority of the members of the governing body then in office` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 276(a) the dissolution of the nonstock corporation is authorized` MEANS
    IF `any members are entitled to vote for the election of members of the governing body or for dissolution under the certificate of incorporation or the bylaws`
    THEN `the dissolution is authorized in accordance with section 275 as performed by the governing body and the members`
    ELSE `the dissolution is authorized by the vote of a majority of the members of the governing body then in office`

-- Section 276(b): a nonstock corporation that has not commenced business: "a majority of the governing body or, if
-- none, a majority of the incorporators" may surrender its rights and franchises by a certificate conforming as nearly
-- as may be to the certificate of section 274.
-- src:1444 | If a nonstock corporation has not commenced the business for which the corporation was organized, a majority of the governing body or, if none, a majority of the incorporators may surrender all of the corporation rights and franchises by filing in the office of the Secretary of State a certificate, executed and acknowledged by a majority of the incorporators or governing body, conforming as nearly as may be to the certificate prescribed by § 274 of this title.
@ref 8 Del. C. § 276(b) (src:1444)
GIVEN `the nonstock corporation has commenced the business for which it was organized` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the corporation has a governing body` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the number of members of the governing body` IS A NUMBER
      `the number of incorporators` IS A NUMBER
      `the number of those who execute and acknowledge the certificate` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 276(b) a majority of the governing body, or of the incorporators, may surrender the rights and franchises` MEANS
    IF `the nonstock corporation has commenced the business for which it was organized`
    THEN JUST FALSE
    ELSE IF `the corporation has a governing body`
         THEN `the vote carries` (`a majority of` (`another base named in the provision` "the governing body")) `the number of those who execute and acknowledge the certificate` `the number of members of the governing body`
         ELSE `the vote carries` (`a majority of` `the incorporators`) `the number of those who execute and acknowledge the certificate` `the number of incorporators`

-- Section 276(c): a nonstock corporation whose certificate limits its duration to a specified date files its certificate
-- of dissolution within 90 days before that date, with the information section 275(f) requires; a failure to file in time
-- does not affect expiry; a certificate of good standing issued after the date has no force or effect. It is the
-- same rule as section 275(f), so section 275(f)'s rules are the rules of section 276(c): they are not written twice.
-- src:1445 | (c) If a nonstock corporation has included in its certificate of incorporation a provision limiting the duration of its existence to a specified date in accordance with § 102(b)(5) of this title, a certificate of dissolution shall be executed, acknowledged and filed in accordance with § 103 of this title within 90 days before such specified date and shall become effective on such specified date. Such certificate of dissolution shall include the information required by § 275(f) of this title. …
-- src:1445 | The failure to timely file a certificate of dissolution pursuant to this subsection with respect to any nonstock corporation shall not affect the expiration of such corporation’s existence on the date specified in its certificate of incorporation pursuant to § 102(b)(5) of this title and shall not eliminate the requirement to file a certificate of dissolution as contemplated by this subsection. …
@ref 8 Del. C. § 276(c) (src:1445)
GIVEN `the date specified in the certificate of incorporation limiting the duration of the corporation's existence` IS A DATE
      `the date the certificate of dissolution is filed` IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 276(c) the nonstock corporation's certificate of dissolution is filed within 90 days before the specified date` MEANS
    `s 275(f) the certificate of dissolution is filed within 90 days before the specified date` WITH `the date specified in the certificate of incorporation limiting the duration of the corporation's existence` IS `the date specified in the certificate of incorporation limiting the duration of the corporation's existence`, `the date the certificate of dissolution is filed` IS `the date the certificate of dissolution is filed`

§§ `s 277 Payment of franchise taxes before dissolution, merger, transfer or conversion`

-- "No corporation shall be dissolved, merged, transferred (without continuing its existence as a corporation of this
-- State) or converted under this chapter until: (1) All franchise taxes due ... have been paid ...; and (2) All annual
-- franchise tax reports ... have been filed ...; notwithstanding the foregoing, if the Secretary of State certifies that an
-- instrument to effect a dissolution, merger, transfer or conversion has been filed in the Secretary of State's office,
-- such corporation shall be dissolved, merged, transferred or converted at the effective time of such instrument."
-- Franchise taxes are chapter 5 of the Law (not among the inputs): whether they are paid is a plain input.
-- src:1449 | No corporation shall be dissolved, merged, transferred (without continuing its existence as a corporation of this State) or converted under this chapter until:
-- src:1450 | (1) All franchise taxes due to or assessable by the State including all franchise taxes due or which would be due or assessable for the entire calendar month during which such dissolution, merger, transfer or conversion becomes effective have been paid by the corporation; and
-- src:1451 | (2) All annual franchise tax reports including a final annual franchise tax report for the year in which such dissolution, merger, transfer or conversion becomes effective have been filed by the corporation;
-- src:1452 | notwithstanding the foregoing, if the Secretary of State certifies that an instrument to effect a dissolution, merger, transfer or conversion has been filed in the Secretary of State’s office, such corporation shall be dissolved, merged, transferred or converted at the effective time of such instrument.
@ref 8 Del. C. § 277 (src:1449-1452)
GIVEN `all franchise taxes due or assessable, including those for the entire calendar month in which the dissolution, merger, transfer or conversion becomes effective, have been paid by the corporation` IS A BOOLEAN
      `all annual franchise tax reports, including a final report for the year in which it becomes effective, have been filed by the corporation` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Secretary of State certifies that an instrument to effect the dissolution, merger, transfer or conversion has been filed` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 277 the corporation may be dissolved, merged, transferred or converted` MEANS
        `the Secretary of State certifies that an instrument to effect the dissolution, merger, transfer or conversion has been filed`
    OR  (    `all franchise taxes due or assessable, including those for the entire calendar month in which the dissolution, merger, transfer or conversion becomes effective, have been paid by the corporation`
         AND `all annual franchise tax reports, including a final report for the year in which it becomes effective, have been filed by the corporation`)
